---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="AI providers"
  description="The provider architecture and current integration status for Veasel Code."
>
  <section class="doc-page page-grid">
    <p class="kicker">FIELD GUIDE / PROVIDERS</p>
    <h1>
      Bring the model
      <br />
      <em>you want to work with.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Veasel Code is being designed around a small provider interface, so model
      connections can grow without tying the session engine to one vendor. The
      adapters are in development and are not yet available in a release.
    </p>
    <div class="doc-panel">
      <h2>Provider work in progress</h2>
      <p>
        Current work is wiring native request and response formats into the V
        backend, validating errors and timeouts, and keeping credentials out of
        session history and logs.
      </p>
      <div
        class="provider-table"
        role="table"
        aria-label="Provider implementation status"
      >
        <div class="provider-table-row provider-table-head" role="row">
          <b role="columnheader">Provider</b>
          <b role="columnheader">Status</b>
          <b role="columnheader">Notes</b>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">OpenAI-compatible</b>
          <span role="cell">In development</span>
          <span role="cell">Configurable endpoint shape</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">Anthropic</b>
          <span role="cell">In development</span>
          <span role="cell">Native Messages API</span>
        </div>
        <div class="provider-table-row" role="row">
          <b role="cell">Gemini</b>
          <span role="cell">In development</span>
          <span role="cell">Native generateContent API</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="callout">
      <strong>Today:</strong> the server provides local session storage and an
      event API. It does not send prompts to an AI provider yet. See the
      <a href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel/blob/main/docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md">
        implementation plan
      </a>
      for current progress.
    </p>
    <a
      class="text-link"
      href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/docs/architecture/`}
    >
      See the architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
